12
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:36,440
And people in cliques are the absolute worst.

13
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:39,820
Because they made us feel more excluded than we already were.

14
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:42,380
I hate break time, too.

15
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:45,220
Yeah, breaks were pretty rough, no doubt.

16
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:47,660
We can practically hear the whispers now.

17
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:51,860
It always felt like kids were pointing out how alone we were.

18
00:00:52,440 --> 00:00:53,660
I mean, they weren't wrong.

19
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:56,420
We hated special events, too.

20
00:00:57,220 --> 00:01:01,580
In fact, I can't remember a single thing we didn't hate in those days.

21
00:01:02,860 --> 00:01:03,740
It sucks.

22
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:07,100
Nobody needs a loser like me around.

23
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:10,300
Can I just die?

24
00:01:14,420 --> 00:01:14,820
Um...

25
00:01:14,820 --> 00:01:17,100
I think we should probably hold off on that.

26
00:01:18,220 --> 00:01:20,660
Not much further down the road, we'll make a friend.

27
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:23,020
He's annoying, though, so heads up.

28
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:28,620
Then we'll meet a kid with great taste of music, a super sweet girl, and a guy who's as tall as he is kind.

29
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:31,840
Oh, and a semi-spineless president and his posse, too.

30
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:36,220
Believe it or not, there are a lot of people who want to be friends with us.

31
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:45,740
Best of all, we'll eventually meet someone who'll cry for us, and laugh at most of our jokes, and keep us in line when we start acting up.

32
00:01:45,740 --> 00:01:52,060
I promise she's out there.

33
