93
00:05:44,880 --> 00:06:01,120
Hey, what were you reading in class just now?

94
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:01,600
Hmm?

95
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,280
A manga?

96
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:05,380
Goethe.

97
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:06,400
Goethe?

98
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:07,580
Um, what is that?

99
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:09,300
A renowned German author.

100
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:11,360
I thought you meant the title at first.

101
00:06:11,820 --> 00:06:12,480
Is it good?

102
00:06:13,420 --> 00:06:15,520
Does your interest mean you like books, too?

103
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:19,860
I won't have my nose in one like that during class, but yeah, books are awesome.

104
00:06:20,340 --> 00:06:21,660
Like Grimm's fairy tales.

105
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:23,400
So Snow White type stuff?

106
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:24,840
Yeah, that's right up my alley.

107
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:27,200
Hmm.

108
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:32,640
I brought books for you to borrow.

109
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,540
No way, you did?

110
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:38,420
There's lots of stories to choose from, so you're bound to like one or two.

111
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:41,640
Wow, thanks so much!

112
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:43,280
That looks like it'll be a fun read.

113
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:43,880
Yep.

114
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:51,320
Oh, do you enjoy books like these, too?

115
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:52,540
You're asking me?

116
00:06:53,340 --> 00:06:53,780
I do.

117
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:57,620
Then, once Ayasaki's finished, you can borrow them as well.

118
00:06:57,860 --> 00:07:00,240
The third story in this collection is really captivating.

119
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:01,840
It's one of my faves.

120
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:03,020
Wait, are you positive?

121
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:03,960
Mm-hmm.

122
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:06,260
Gosh, thank you!

123
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:07,860
Sure, don't mention it.

124
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:09,200
Hmm?

125
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:12,980
You know, you have great taste!

126
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:14,720
I like them all.

127
00:07:15,380 --> 00:07:16,700
Good, because they brought more.

128
00:07:16,980 --> 00:07:19,320
Wow, you're like a one-man library.

129
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:20,340
That's amazing!

130
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:21,940
How many books do you own?

131
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:23,620
My parents own most of these.

132
00:07:23,940 --> 00:07:26,120
We have a room filled wall-to-wall with them back home.

133
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:28,260
That sounds insane!

134
00:07:28,460 --> 00:07:29,400
I wish I could see.

135
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:31,680
You can, if you want to.

136
00:07:33,380 --> 00:07:34,620
Oh, did I say that?

137
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:36,220
I didn't mean anything weird!

138
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:37,800
Yeah, of course.

139
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:39,080
Neither did I.

140
00:07:42,980 --> 00:07:46,340
It is filled wall-to-wall!

141
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:48,920
We don't clean this room much.

142
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:50,620
I'm sorry that it's so dusty.

143
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:53,500
You okay?

144
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:55,280
Yes, I'm fine.

145
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:57,460
I was just trying to pull down this book is all.

146
00:07:57,940 --> 00:07:59,920
I should have asked before I touched, though.

147
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:03,080
Won't find many books older than that one.

148
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:04,160
Do you remember the premise?

149
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:07,520
I think it's about the day before the world ends.

150
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:08,340
Oh.

151
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:11,120
As in the whole world or Japan?

152
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:13,600
I believe it's the whole world.

153
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:15,020
So they're in panic mode.

154
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,620
If everything was going up in smoke the next day,

155
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:20,360
most people would probably just lie around and wait for it.

156
00:08:20,940 --> 00:08:21,800
Oh, not me!

157
00:08:22,020 --> 00:08:24,000
I'd spend the whole day blowing through my money,

158
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:25,540
then load up on desserts!

159
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:28,080
It's your final day on Earth,

160
00:08:28,140 --> 00:08:29,600
and you're gonna stuff your face?!

161
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:31,620
There's so much I haven't tried,

162
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:33,160
so I might as well.

163
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:34,020
Huh.

164
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:39,200
Your hair, it's up higher than it usually is, right?

165
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:43,500
Yeah, I just felt like it.

166
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:45,720
Nice call. Looks good.

167
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:46,840
You think so?

168
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:56,300
Cute people could get away with murder

169
00:08:56,300 --> 00:08:57,580
and look cute doing it.

170
00:08:57,740 --> 00:09:00,400
But I guess you wouldn't get where I'm coming from, huh?

171
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:03,220
Mind if I borrow you for a second?

172
00:09:03,620 --> 00:09:04,240
Pretty please?

173
00:09:05,940 --> 00:09:07,360
Thanks for lending me these.

174
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:08,840
I read every last page.

175
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:10,660
There was no need to rush through them.

176
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:11,820
I didn't.

177
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:14,360
They were so entertaining that I couldn't put them down.

178
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:16,460
And that one book made me realize

179
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:18,120
how much I don't want the world to end.

180
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:20,000
What about your big sweets binge?

181
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:22,240
There are way more important things than sweets

182
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:23,280
when it's Judgment Day!

183
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:30,000
So, you know,

184
00:09:30,420 --> 00:09:32,200
